  <section id="guide" class="relative w-full">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
      <header class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mb-2 text-lightblue">A Practical Field Guide to Nitrox Diving in Bali</h2>
        <p class="text-white/80">This isn't just about what nitrox is; it's about how to use it to unlock Bali's best underwater experiences. From the thriving reefs of Nusa Penida to the iconic USAT Liberty wreck, enriched air is the tool for the serious diver.</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
        
        <p>For the certified diver, nitrox (or Enriched Air Nitrox - EANx) is one of the most practical upgrades to your skill set. By increasing the oxygen percentage and reducing the nitrogen in your breathing gas, you gain two significant advantages: longer no-decompression limits (NDLs) and shorter required surface intervals. In a destination like Bali, where world-class dive sites are clustered together, this means more time underwater and less time waiting on the boat.</p>

        <h3 class="text-gold"><i class="fa-solid fa-list-check mr-2"></i>Key Strategic Takeaways</h3>
        <ul class="marker:text-gold space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Maximize Repetitive Dives:</strong> Nitrox significantly reduces your residual nitrogen loading, making your second and third dives of the day longer and safer.</li>
            <li><strong>Unlock Deeper Profiles:</strong> Safely extend your time in the 18-30 meter ($60-100$ ft) range, perfect for exploring Bali’s famous walls, wrecks, and deeper reefs where marine life thrives.</li>
            <li><strong>Enhance Safety Margins:</strong> Many experienced divers use nitrox but follow air tables on their computer for an extra layer of conservatism, reducing the risk of decompression sickness.</li>
            <li><strong>Invest in Experience:</strong> The small surcharge for a nitrox fill is a direct investment in more valuable underwater time, especially for photographers and marine life enthusiasts.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-lightblue"><i class="fa-solid fa-map-location-dot mr-2"></i>Prime Nitrox Dive Locations in Bali</h3>
        <p>Choosing the right gas for the right dive is key. Here’s how nitrox offers a distinct advantage at Bali’s top sites:</p>
        
        <div class="p-4 border border-white/10 rounded-xl bg-white/5 mb-4">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-lg text-white">Nusa Penida (Manta Point, Crystal Bay, SD Point)</h4>
          <p class="mt-2 text-white/80"><strong>The Objective:</strong> Encountering majestic Manta Rays and the elusive Mola mola (oceanic sunfish), and enjoying thrilling drift dives over vibrant coral gardens. Dives are typically in the 20-30 meter range.<br>
          <strong>Nitrox Advantage:</strong> When the mantas are circling at a cleaning station or you're scanning the deep blue for a Mola, the last thing you want is your computer signaling low NDL. Nitrox gives you that crucial extra bottom time to wait for the perfect encounter and provides a safety buffer during energetic drift dives.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 border border-white/10 rounded-xl bg-white/5 mb-4">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-lg text-white">Tulamben (USAT Liberty Wreck, The Drop-Off)</h4>
          <p class="mt-2 text-white/80"><strong>The Objective:</strong> Exploring the immense 120-meter-long USAT Liberty shipwreck and the dramatic vertical wall nearby. Photographers flock here for both wide-angle and macro subjects.<br>
          <strong>Nitrox Advantage:</strong> The Liberty Wreck is a multi-level playground. To truly appreciate its scale—from the shallowest point at 5 meters to the stern at nearly 30 meters—you need time. Nitrox is almost essential here for a thorough exploration on a single dive, allowing you to linger in the swim-throughs and hunt for pygmy seahorses without constantly checking your NDL.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 border border-white/10 rounded-xl bg-white/5">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-lg text-white">Amed & Padang Bai (The Japanese Wreck, Blue Lagoon)</h4>
          <p class="mt-2 text-white/80"><strong>The Objective:</strong> Macro photography, muck diving, and relaxed reef exploration. These areas are perfect for two- or three-dive days focused on finding unique critters like frogfish, ghost pipefish, and nudibranchs.<br>
          <strong>Nitrox Advantage:</strong> This is where nitrox shines for repetitive diving. Your second and third dives will have significantly longer available bottom times compared to diving on air, meaning more opportunity to find that rare creature your guide pointed out without cutting the dive short.</p>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-lightblue"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved mr-2"></i>Safety & Best Practices: The Non-Negotiables</h3>
        <p>Using nitrox is safe and straightforward, but it demands respect and adherence to procedure. Your certification course covers this in detail, but here are the golden rules:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li><strong class="text-white"><i class="fa-solid fa-gauge-high mr-2 text-gold"></i>Analyze Your Gas:</strong> Never assume the mix in your tank is correct. You are responsible for personally using an oxygen analyzer to check the percentage ($O_2\%$) and signing for it.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white"><i class="fa-solid fa-computer mr-2 text-gold"></i>Set Your Computer:</strong> Before every dive, ensure your dive computer is set to the correct oxygen percentage. Failure to do so negates the benefits and is extremely dangerous.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white"><i class="fa-solid fa-water-ladder mr-2 text-gold"></i>Respect Your MOD:</strong> Understand and respect your Maximum Operating Depth (MOD) for your specific mix. Descending below this depth exposes you to the risk of Central Nervous System (CNS) oxygen toxicity. Your guide will plan the dive profile accordingly, but you are the ultimate guardian of your own safety.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-accent" id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          
          <div class="border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 bg-white/5">
            <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
              <span class="font-semibold">Is nitrox suitable for beginners?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down text-sm"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden mt-3 text-white/80">Yes, once you have your Open Water certification, the Enriched Air (Nitrox) course is a great next step. It's a non-technical specialty that focuses on theory and safety procedures. Diving with nitrox under guidance is very safe and beneficial, even for relatively new divers.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 bg-white/5">
            <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
              <span class="font-semibold">What’s the ideal season for nitrox diving in Bali?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down text-sm"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden mt-3 text-white/80">The dry season, from April to November, typically offers the best surface conditions and visibility. However, Bali offers year-round diving. Nitrox is particularly useful on any day you plan multiple dives, regardless of the season.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 bg-white/5">
            <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
              <span class="font-semibold">How much extra does a nitrox tank cost in Bali?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down text-sm"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden mt-3 text-white/80">The surcharge for a nitrox fill is generally modest, often ranging from $5 to $10 USD per tank. Considering the benefits of extended bottom time and shorter surface intervals, most divers find it to be a worthwhile investment in their dive day.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 bg-white/5">
            <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
              <span class="font-semibold">Do I need my own special gear for nitrox?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down text-sm"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden mt-3 text-white/80">You need a nitrox-compatible dive computer. While most modern regulators and BCDs are fine for recreational nitrox (up to 40% oxygen), your computer is essential for tracking your exposure. You'll also use an oxygen analyzer, which the dive shop provides, to verify your gas mix before diving.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 bg-white/5">
            <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden')">
              <span class="font-semibold">Can I get nitrox certified in Bali?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down text-sm"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden mt-3 text-white/80">Absolutely. Bali is an excellent place to take the PADI Enriched Air (Nitrox) Diver course. It's typically a one-day course with no complex in-water skills, focusing on gas management theory. You can easily combine it with your first day of diving.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="mt-8 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-sm text-white/80">
